  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$,\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is odd **or** even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is odd }}_{⏟}}_{O}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{E},\n$$\n\nthat is, $O∨E.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $y$ is negative **or** positive. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{y\\text{ is negative }}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{y\\text{ is positive }}_{⏟}}_{P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is odd or even}}_{⏟}}_{O\\,∨\\,E}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{x\\text{ is negative or positive }}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∨\\,P},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(O∨E)∧(N∨P).$",
